 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Keep it short, thank the staff, and ask for different dish rather than complaining in front of others. No, ask the chef in passing at some point during the meal. They'll usually take it well and can fix it. Explain you were just eating and didn't want to interrupt. They usually understand. Some people are naturally dramatic about food. Others genuinely have an allergy or intolerance. It' better to be safe than sorry.",
